## Appendix H: Economic Layer

### H.1 Equity-Adjusted ICER

Let \(C\) and \(Q\) be cost and QALYs. The equity-adjusted ICER is
\[
\text{ICER}_{\text{equity}}
=
\frac{C - C_0}{
\sum_{A} w_A Q_A - Q_0
}.
\]
For interpretability, either normalize \(\sum_A w_A = 1\) or explicitly state the QALY scaling convention.

### H.2 Weight Specifications

Proportional:
\[
w_A = \frac{N_{\text{total}}}{k \cdot n_A}.
\]
Disparity-based:
\[
w_A = \frac{\max_B h_B}{h_A}.
\]
Atkinson:
\[
w_A = \left(\frac{\bar{h}}{h_A}\right)^{\epsilon}.
\]

### H.3 Incentive Compatibility

Assume \(C(q)\) is nondecreasing. The pricing rule is
\[
R(q)
=
R_{\text{base}}
\left(
1
+
\alpha \mathbf{1}\{q \geq q_1\}
+
\beta \mathbf{1}\{q \geq q_2\}
+
\gamma \mathbf{1}\{q \geq q_3\}
\right).
\]
If
\[
\alpha R_{\text{base}} \geq C(q_1) - C(0),
\]
\[
\beta R_{\text{base}} \geq C(q_2) - C(q_1),
\]
\[
\gamma R_{\text{base}} \geq C(q_3) - C(q_2),
\]
then \(q^* = q_3\) is globally optimal.

*Proof.*
\[
\Pi(q) = R(q) - C(q).
\]
The conditions imply
\[
\Pi(q_1) \geq \Pi(0),\quad
\Pi(q_2) \geq \Pi(q_1),\quad
\Pi(q_3) \geq \Pi(q_2).
\]
Because \(C\) is nondecreasing, for \(q \in (q_i, q_{i+1})\),
\[
R(q) = R(q_i),\qquad
C(q) \geq C(q_i),
\]
so \(\Pi(q) \leq \Pi(q_i)\). Hence \(\Pi(q_3) \geq \Pi(q)\) for all \(q \in [0,1]\). \(\square\)

If \(C\) is not monotone, the stronger global conditions are
\[
\Pi(q_3)
\geq
\max\{\Pi(0), \Pi(q_1), \Pi(q_2)\},
\]
together with interval checks.

